  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4a2b061e491659d4e8424ca22aacc1c7, type: 3}
  m_Name: Read_ZoneProfile_Construction_Mid
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Hecton8.World.WorldExpeditionLoopProfile
  profileId: loop.profile.construction.mid
  profileLabel: Construction Mid Read
  entryBeat: Sockets, frames, and awkward geometry immediately suggest possible improvement.
  routineBeat: The player reads what is easy to place, what is blocked, and what
    could become useful later.
  reliefBeat: A clean work pocket offers a moment of clarity in otherwise messy space.
  pressureBeat: Pressure comes from obstruction, poor angles, and the cost of investing
    here.
  payoffBeat: 'The reward is a better place: easier travel, better support, or a
    smarter foothold.'
  exitBeat: The player can leave after learning enough, even if they build nothing
    yet.
  playerFreedomRule: Construction is optional leverage, not a required progression
    step.
  softProgressionPull: The zone suggests that building here could improve later runs.
  optionalDetourRule: Even without building, the player should understand why this
    spot matters.
  returnLogic: The place should stay memorable as a future improvement opportunity.
  masteryLogic: Mastery means spotting where investment pays off and where it does
    not.
  playerPromise: A place where player agency can reshape local quality of life.
  routeMemoryRule: Memory should hold onto the best socket, the main blocker, and
    the clearest working angle.
  failureMode: If building here changes nothing meaningful, the area feels fake.
